<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - April 21.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - April 21.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for April 21. In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Apr    228.50    232.00    232.50     233.50</p>
<p>    May    228.50    232.00    232.50     233.50</p>
<p>    Jun    223.50    227.00    227.50     232.00</p>
<p>    Jul    219.50    223.00    223.50     229.50</p>
<p>    Aug    218.50    222.00    222.50     228.50</p>
<p>    Sept   218.50    222.00    222.50     228.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$4.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	199.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  174.50	    Port Adelaide	 176.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     174.75	    Port Giles	    176.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	172.50	    Wallaroo		174.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    171.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     174.50	    Port Lincoln	  177.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   175.00	    Thevenard	     172.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 174.00	     Esperance	    179.25</p>
<p>    Portland	175.00	     Albany		 180.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    182.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    180.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT).  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
